+# Spec Delta: IBrowserFingerService.GetClientHubIdAsync
+
+Status: implemented
+
+## Objective
+Expose the client hub id (the per-browser id that `ClientHub` / `hub.js` stores) through
+`IBrowserFingerService` so components and services can read it from C#.
+
+## Current Behavior
+`IBrowserFingerService` only provides `GetFingerCodeAsync`. `hub.js` keeps the client id in
+`localStorage['bb_hub_connection_id']`, but C# code has no way to read it.
+
+## New Behavior
+- `Task<string?> GetClientHubIdAsync(CancellationToken token = default)` on `IBrowserFingerService`.
+- `DefaultBrowserFingerService` calls the JS function `getClientHubId` in `modules/utility.js`.
+- `getClientHubId()` returns `localStorage.getItem('bb_hub_connection_id')`, or `null` if it is not set.
+
+## Success Criteria
+- `test/UnitTest/Services/BrowserFingerServiceTest.cs` `GetClientHubIdAsync_Ok` passes.
+- `GetFingerCodeAsync` behavior and its test are unchanged.
+
+## Boundaries
+- No new dependencies; reuse the existing `utility.js` module.
